---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---
<BaseLayout title="What POYARA Can Build — Websites, Software & Interactive 3D" description="Business websites, digital product prototypes, interactive 3D demos and visual experiences built around real customer problems.">
  <section class="page-header wrap solutions-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">SOLUTIONS / START WITH THE PROBLEM</p>
    <h1>Make the complex<br /><em>usable.</em></h1>
    <p>POYARA helps businesses and founders make their websites, products, technical stories and spatial ideas useful to the people who need them.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap solutions-section" aria-labelledby="solutions-heading">
    <div class="solutions-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">WHERE WE CAN HELP</p>
      <h2 id="solutions-heading">Start with the need.<br /><em>Build the answer.</em></h2>
      <p>Each engagement begins with a specific audience and a useful first deliverable—not a promise to build an entire platform.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="solution-cases">
      <article id="web-experiences" class="solution-case">
        <div class="solution-case-number"><span>01 / PRESENT</span><span>FOR BUSINESSES, BRANDS & ARCHITECTS</span></div>
        <div class="solution-case-main">
          <div>
            <h3>Your website needs to make a strong first impression—and do a job.</h3>
            <p>A beautiful website is only the beginning. Give people a clear way to understand your business, inspect your work and take the next step. Where it helps, motion, 3D and interactive elements can explain more than static pages.</p>
            <ul class="solution-outputs">
              <li>Responsive company websites, portfolio sites and landing pages</li>
              <li>Purpose-built interfaces, editorial motion and interactive showcases</li>
              <li>Practical site architecture, content structure and launch preparation</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class="solution-proof">
            <p class="eyebrow">SEE THE WORK IN A BROWSER</p>
            <strong>Real website previews across architecture, hospitality and visual storytelling.</strong>
            <a href={withBase('websites/')}>Explore the website portfolio <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article id="technical-demonstration" class="solution-case">
        <div class="solution-case-number"><span>02 / EXPLAIN</span><span>FOR TECHNICAL & PRODUCT TEAMS</span></div>
        <div class="solution-case-main">
          <div>
            <h3>People can't understand your product from a static image.</h3>
            <p>Let customers, trainees or collaborators explore the equipment, mechanism or scientific process themselves. Show parts, motion and relationships instead of relying on a finished render alone.</p>
            <ul class="solution-outputs">
              <li>Interactive 3D product or equipment presentation</li>
              <li>Exploded views, functional motion and guided explanations</li>
              <li>Technical or scientific animation when interaction is not the right format</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class="solution-proof">
            <p class="eyebrow">A POSSIBLE FIRST DELIVERABLE</p>
            <strong>A browser-based demonstration that someone can inspect.</strong>
            <a href={withBase('work/industrial-pump-demo/')}>Inspect the industrial-pump example <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article id="software-prototype" class="solution-case">
        <div class="solution-case-number"><span>03 / TEST</span><span>FOR FOUNDERS & OPERATORS</span></div>
        <div class="solution-case-main">
          <div>
            <h3>You know the workflow. You need to test the software.</h3>
            <p>Turn a service idea or an awkward operational process into a usable prototype. Make the roles, rules and decisions visible before committing to a larger software build.</p>
            <ul class="solution-outputs">
              <li>A focused interface and connected user journey</li>
              <li>Working logic for the decisions that matter</li>
              <li>A prototype with clear questions for a real-world test</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class="solution-proof">
            <p class="eyebrow">A POSSIBLE FIRST DELIVERABLE</p>
            <strong>An end-to-end working flow, ready to put in front of users.</strong>
            <a href={withBase('work/mizato/')}>Explore the Mizato product study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article id="spatial-experience" class="solution-case">
        <div class="solution-case-number"><span>04 / VISUALIZE</span><span>FOR BRANDS, DESIGNERS & RETAILERS</span></div>
        <div class="solution-case-main">
          <div>
            <h3>Customers need to see how something fits their world.</h3>
            <p>Move beyond a catalog image. An interactive spatial experience can let people explore scale, placement and product variations in the context of their own decision.</p>
            <ul class="solution-outputs">
              <li>Browser-based AR or real-time 3D experience</li>
              <li>Product placement, scale or configuration interactions</li>
              <li>A testable experience before catalog-scale production</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class="solution-proof">
            <p class="eyebrow">A POSSIBLE FIRST DELIVERABLE</p>
            <strong>A spatial demo someone can open on a compatible device.</strong>
            <a href={withBase('work/chido/')}>Explore the Chido AR experiment <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="solution-next section-band">
    <div class="wrap solution-next-inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">START SMALL, LEARN EARLY</p>
        <h2>You don't need a perfect brief.</h2>
        <p>Describe who needs to use or understand something, what is difficult today and what a useful first test would prove. We can define a sensible prototype boundary from there.</p>
        <div class="inline-actions">
          <a class="primary-button" href={withBase('contact/')}>Discuss a specific problem <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href={withBase('work/')}>See the public work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="case-meta">
        <p class="eyebrow">HOW A FIRST ENGAGEMENT WORKS</p>
        <div><span>01 / Frame</span><strong>Audience, decision and constraints</strong></div>
        <div><span>02 / Scope</span><strong>One useful, inspectable deliverable</strong></div>
        <div><span>03 / Build</span><strong>A working interactive or visual prototype</strong></div>
        <div><span>04 / Review</span><strong>Evidence, limitations and the next decision</strong></div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
